                <pb facs="1325" n="1201" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg1201"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.602 Ot 81/258: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-04-12T12:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 12,
                                1923—noon</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received April 12—11:09
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>104. French High Commissioner presented yesterday to Angora representative formal
                    note of protest against adoption of the Chester project by Assembly. Am
                    following situation closely and will telegraph details later.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
